11. Promotion Across Environments

I strongly recommend AMI promotion rather than rebuilding the same image independently for every environment.

                    Golden AMI
                        |
                        ▼
                      DEV
                        |
                 Validation
                        |
                        ▼
                      UAT
                        |
                 Validation
                        |
                        ▼
                     PROD
                        |
                 Production

Or:

Build
  ↓
DEV
  ↓
Security Validation
  ↓
UAT
  ↓
Application Validation
  ↓
Production Approval
  ↓
PROD

The same AMI artifact should ideally move through environments.

That gives you:

Build once → validate → promote

rather than:

Build separately → DEV → build again → UAT → build again → PROD

12. Continuous Compliance

Once the EC2 instance is deployed, the responsibility doesn't stop.

You need a feedback loop.

                    Production EC2
                          |
          +---------------+---------------+
          |               |               |
          ▼               ▼               ▼
      Patch Mgmt      Security Hub     CloudWatch
          |               |               |
          ▼               ▼               ▼
     Compliance       Findings        Monitoring
          |               |               |
          +---------------+---------------+
                          |
                          ▼
                  Security Finding
                          |
                          ▼
                   Remediation
                          |
                          ▼
                  Image Rebuild

This is important because an AMI can be compliant on Day 1 but drift on Day 90.

